Telerik's knowledge base lists two prerequisites for the attack: the attacker "can break the RadAsyncUpload encryption (or have prior knowledge of your custom encryption keys)", and the control's type whitelisting is not enabled. Telerik rates the encryption as breakable up to R2 2017 SP1 and as needing the keys from R2 2017 SP2; type whitelisting is unavailable before R3 2019 SP1, opt-in in that release and enabled by default from R1 2020 (2020.1.114), and Telerik recommends its RadAsyncUpload security settings on every version ([Progress Telerik](https://www.telerik.com/products/aspnet-ajax/documentation/knowledge-base/common-allows-javascriptserializer-deserialization)). AhnLab's mitigation is the upgrade to 2020.1.114 or later, the latest version where possible ([AhnLab ASEC, 2026-09-27](https://asec.ahnlab.com/en/95561/)).
